			<div class="content" id="post-content-4764654">
									

<div>
<div style="text-align: center;">
<p><strong>The medium is the message.</strong><br />
<strong>- Marshall McLuhan</strong></p>
</div>
</div>
<p>I've been working on this for <em>months.</em></p>
<p>I've written and published two tales totalling about twenty-three thousand words and a joke SCP in that time. I've also written and <em>not</em> published three shorter tales and another complete SCP (which is now likely imminent). This idea grew in the execution, and it's been both rewarding and infuriating watching it get away from me then trying to rein it back in.</p>
<p>In the end, you can only rein so much. Dr. Zwist knows that all too well.</p>
<p>Thanks to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/grigori-karpin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4558017); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4558017&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1604090238" alt="Grigori Karpin" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4558017)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/grigori-karpin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4558017); return false;">Grigori Karpin</a></span> and his excellent, conscientious crit for forcing me to rein it in further than I thought I could! I will <em>fight you</em> if you think there are still extraneous sections to this. You should see my cutting room floor! Because you <em>can't.</em></p>
<p><strong>Things What Might Look Like Mistakes but Aren't:</strong><br />
1. Lots of Thaumiels are compound anomalies;<br />
2. Hiemal anomalies contain each other. This one does not. It's not Hiemal;<br />
3. Yes, SCP-006 is Overseer-eyes only. Seriously. Go look (or don't, <em>yawn</em>);<br />
4. No, you're not meant to be able to read all the text on a few of these pics. What can be reasonably faked at 300px will look like hot garbage at 500, when said faker is amateur at best;<br />
5. Uhhhh&#8230; they <em>did</em> have metal bottle caps in 1895!</p>
